{
  "raw": {
    "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Vice-President-for-Enrollment-Management_JR100252": {
      "title": "Vice President for Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Ohio Northern University, an independent, selective, comprehensive university located in Northwest, Ohio, announces the search for a strategic Vice President for Enrollment Management (VPEM). The Vice President for Enrollment Management serves as a key member of the President’s Cabinet, reporting directly to the President. This senior leadership role provides strategic oversight and direction for all enrollment management operations, ensuring alignment with the University’s mission, financial objectives, and commitment to building an academically strong and multi-talented student body. Job Description : THE POSITION The Vice President for Enrollment Management will provide visible, positive, and approachable leadership to an office of 15 professional staff, including four direct reports. The VPEM is responsible for leading the University’s enrollment strategy, encompassing student recruitment, admissions, financial aid, and enrollment planning. Working collaboratively, the Vice President drives initiatives to meet or exceed enrollment targets, achieve net tuition revenue goals, and enhance the quality and breadth of applicant pools. Through collaborative partnerships across the University, especially with the Vice President for Financial Affairs (VPFA), the Provost, and the Athletic Director, the VPEM ensures a coordinated, data-driven approach to recruiting, retaining, and graduating students from varied backgrounds. Full Position Announcement: https://nessearches.com/onu-vpem/ COMPENSATION Compensation for the position will be competitive and based on the skills and experience of the selected candidate and the agreed upon portfolio of responsibilities; consult with the NES search team for insights. Additionally, Ohio Northern University offers a comprehensive package of benefits. Given the nature of this visible campus and community-based leadership position, the selected candidate will be expected to reside in or near Ada, Ohio. To Apply NES , a higher education search firm specializing in enrollment management searches, is assisting Ohio Northern in identifying the University's next Vice President for Enrollment Management. For more information, or to nominate someone for this position, contact Suzi Nam ( suzi.nam@nessearches.com ) or Laura Robinson ( laura.robinson@nessearches.com ). All conversations will remain confidential unless otherwise stated and agreed. Interested candidates should submit a résumé and a letter of interest describing their unique qualifications for the Vice President for Enrollment Management position at Ohio Northern University. Candidates should also provide the names and contact information of at least five professional references. For confidentiality, references will not be contacted without permission. For best consideration, all application materials should be submitted electronically to ONU@nessearches.com by September 23, 2025. The position is campus-based and the preferred start date is January of 2026. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."
    },
    "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Coordinator-for-the-Department-of-Art---Communication---the-Department-of-Performing-Arts_JR100237": {
      "title": "Coordinator for the Department of Art & Communication & the Department of Performing Arts",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: This position is primarily responsible for supporting the functions of the academic programs of Art & Design, Communication & Media, Music, Musical Theatre, and Theatre. Chief tasks include general administrative functions, assisting students and faculty, maintaining budgets, and other specific tasks as assigned. Job Description : ● Perform all financial activities associated with school and program accounts, including budget tracking and auditing, credit card purchases and reconciliation, submission of purchase orders, etc. ● Complete and submit Semester Course Offerings schedules and changes to the Registrar ● Maintain student records and financial records ● Maintain and order office and teaching supplies ● Complete adjunct contract requests in coordination with Director and Department Chair ● Maintain syllabi, faculty office hours, and department meeting minutes electronically ● Hire, schedule, and supervise student workers ● Assist with organization of department and program events ● Support various needs of students and faculty ● Other duties as assigned ● Coordinate international and national guest artist visits  ● Apply for licensure and rights for all in-house productions; acquire and return scripts and scores to licensing companies. ● Attend Department and Program meetings and take accurate and thorough documentation of meetings. ● Draft, maintain and submit practicum credit forms to the Registrar’s oﬃce for departmental productions. ● Manage all keys for PAC building, bulletin boards and directories ● Schedule PAC classrooms for both academic and non-academic purposes. Percentage Of Total Time: 30%   Responsibility / Duty:  Monitor department budget and track expenses. Responsible for purchasing for the department, overseeing department travel and credit charges.   Percentage Of Total Time: 20%   Responsibility / Duty:  Responsible for department schedules: Meetings, classroom assignments, assistance with semester course assignments and load documents   Percentage Of Total Time: 30%   Responsibility / Duty:  Department-specific accounting/planning, such as planning for travel for guest artists, keep department files and records.   Percentage Of Total Time: 20%   Responsibility / Duty:  Primary contact with and provides necessary department information to the university, deans’, registrar’s and controller’s offices. Required Skills: ● Excellent communication, organization, and time management skills ● Excellent attention to detail ● Knowledge of standard office policies and procedures ● Knowledge of University administrative policies ● Proficiency in Microsoft Office products ● Ability to learn and work with various software programs ● Strong initiative skills ● Ability to manage and supervise student workers ● Ability to perform complex procedures using appropriate analytic skills Minimum Qualifications: ● Bachelor’s Degree or equivalent experience ● At least two to five years of similar office experience Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."
