    "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Public-Safety-Officer_JR100183": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: This position is responsible for protecting members of the University Community, maintaining order, enforcing policies and procedures, rules and regulations of the Ohio Northern University. Public Safety officers may be assigned to uniform or plainclothes details. Shift scheduling changes periodically, sometimes with little advanced notice in emergency situations. Duties require initiative, resourcefulness and the ability to analyze situations and in emergencies to adopt a quick, effective and responsible course of action. The work involves frequent contact with the public and requires the ability to deal with persons in tense situations where attitudes and relations are strained. Job Description : - Patrols designated areas via motor vehicle, bicycle or on foot to detect criminal activity; inspects doors, windows and premises of University buildings and properties; to detect suspicious vehicles, persons or situations ; maintains high visibility. - Responds to calls for service including domestic situations, assaults, burglaries, thefts, property damage, alarms, bomb threats, natural disasters that affect campus, public service duties such as escorts, vehicle lockouts and door unlocks. - Conducts preliminary/ follow up investigations of complaints or incidents on University property, involving University students, faculty, staff or visitors to campus. - Take fingerprints for background checks. - May be asked to testify in court when subpoenaed; escort law enforcement officers or investigators on campus for various situations; provides assistance or backup to public service agencies including fire and EMS on campus and provide twenty-four hour service to Ohio Northern University. - Operates a variety of standard and specialized equipment and tools associated with public safety including vehicles, OC spray, handcuffs, asp baton, flashlights, fire extinguishers, photographic equipment, telephones, radios, desktop computers, tablets and general office equipment. - Inspects and maintains assigned vehicles and related equipment assigned to public safety vehicles. - Follows safety procedures, utilizes equipment, monitors work environment to ensure the safety of University faculty, staff,students and visitors; Performs driving functions in a safe and efficient manner under various conditions and in adverse weather conditions. - Prepares and completes required forms, reports, correspondence, logs, event reports, damage reports, narratives, missing persons reports, parking registrations and enforces parking regulations on all University lots. - Enters reports directly into ReportExec RMS, using a computer and its accompanying equipment such as a computer and mouse. - Communicates in person, via telephone and/or radio, provides assistance and information to those needing help. - Creates/ maintains positive public relations with the University community and visitors to our campus; Maintains and promotes peace and order; Provides education and information regarding University policies and procedures, personal safety, drug abuse and the law, alcohol laws, crime prevention and other public safety issues. - Attends shift meetings, training sessions both on and off campus, seminars as required to remain knowledgeable of departmental/ University operations and activities, to promote improved job performance and to stay current with trends in the field of public safety. - Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: - High school diploma or GED equivalent - Possess a valid Ohio driver's license - Must be at least 21 years of age - Must be able to successfully complete an approved Ohio Peace Officer Training Private Security Firearms Course within 90 days of employment or a time approved by the Chief of Public Safety if the time exceeds the 90 days based on class availability. Preferred Qualifications: - Ohio Peace Officer training or military equivalent experience - Fire service or EMS background - Professional Security Officer certifications Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."
    },
    "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Vice-President-of-Enrollment-Operations---Slate-Expert_JR100181": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President of Enrollment Operations & Slate Expert",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Ohio Northern University invites applications for the position of Assistant Vice President (AVP) of Enrollment Operations and Slate Expert. Reporting directly to the Vice President for Enrollment, this high-level leadership role serves as a core member of the Enrollment Management (EM) leadership team, alongside the Associate VP of Enrollment/Director of Financial Aid, the Senior Director of Enrollment Communications, and the Director of Admissions. The AVP Enrollment Operations/Slate Expert provides strategic vision, technological leadership, and administrative oversight for all enrollment infrastructure, data integrity, and systems integration. Acting as the university's primary Slate CRM expert, this position manages the technological framework that drives recruitment, selection, and enrollment. The AVP directly supervises the Director of Admissions Operations and one Executive Admissions Assistant, who manage the day-to-day admissions and application processing within Slate and oversee the data exchange with Banner. Additionally, this role will play a critical, hands-on leadership role in the university’s upcoming institutional upgrade: Ohio Northern University will be transitioning its Student Information System (SIS) to Workday in the very near future. The AVP will spearhead the enrollment operations strategy to ensure a seamless data transition from Slate to Workday, safeguarding data governance and operational continuity. Job Description : Strategic Enrollment Leadership & Collaboration Serve as a key member of the Enrollment Management leadership team, participating in enrollment leadership meetings and strategic planning discussions to shape the university's recruitment and enrollment strategies. Foster a culture focused on collaboration, innovation, operational excellence, and continuous improvement across the division. Collaborate effectively with stakeholders across Enrollment Management, Marketing, Financial Aid, Institutional Research, and Information Technologies, Academics, Athletics, etc.. Provide strategic analysis of enrollment management data and lead continuous improvements in Slate business processes to support undergraduate, graduate, and professional enrollment teams. Work closely with the Vice President for Enrollment Management to prioritize and provide all key enrollment-related reports, dashboards, queries, portals, etc. to optimize use of the CRM and improve efficiencies Slate CRM Expert Administration & Innovation Serve as the lead professional on technology matters, including processing, reporting, data extraction, and system configuration within Technolutions Slate. Build, maintain, and enhance the Slate environment—including forms, fields, workflows, queries, rules, populations, permissions, realms, reader configurations, and portals—to optimize outreach and streamline business processes. Stay current with new Slate features, enhancements, and industry best practices; explore creative ideas to implement and improve the Slate environment. Manage the annual cycle prep steps for each part of the admissions and recruitment cycle. Work with territory managers to identify ways in which Slate can be better utilized to refine current recruitment strategies and travel. Collaborate with the application review coordinator to identify application loads for staff, manage Reader Assignments in Slate, keep abreast of reading progress, and reallocate as necessary. System Transition, Integration & Data Integrity Lead the upcoming strategic transition from the current Banner SIS infrastructure to Workday over the next two years, serving as the primary enrollment architect for a seamless data transition between Slate and Workday. Oversee data uploads, data exchanges, and integrations from vendors and external partners (such as the Common Application), ensuring data accuracy, completeness, and consistency. Partner closely with Information Technology and Enrollment Systems to maintain rigid data integrity standards across the Slate CRM and the SIS. Collaborate with Institutional Research and campus partners to align reporting standards, data governance practices, and census reporting. Perform regular audits for data integrity; troubleshoot system issues, identify root causes, and facilitate communication with staff and stakeholders. Serve as the ultimate back-up for all integration, data upload, decision confirmation, and release processes. Enrollment Reporting & Analytics Generate and refine enrollment reports and dashboards tracking key performance indicators across the admissions funnel to support data-informed decision-making. Analyze recruitment, application, admission, and enrollment trends to provide actionable insights, predictive modeling, and strategic recommendations to university leadership, cabinet members, and the Board of Trustees. Assist with enrollment communication initiatives by providing audience segmentation, list management, and campaign reporting. External Vendor Management & Pipeline Alignment Oversee the secure ingestion and deployment of external data lists into Slate, tracking source effectiveness to evaluate lead-to-application conversion rates and maximize vendor ROI. Maintain close, transparent communication with the Vice President for Enrollment Management regarding vendor performance, lead volume metrics, and contract management. Ensure all vendor integrations and data acquisitions explicitly align with the university’s Strategic Enrollment Plan (SEP), targeting key geographic markets, academic profiles, and diversity initiatives to meet institutional enrollment goals. Team Supervision & Professional Development Supervise, mentor, and evaluate the Director of Admissions Operations and one Executive Admissions Assistant, providing work prioritization, performance management, and professional growth opportunities. Provide day-to-day troubleshooting, training, and mentoring for all Slate users across campus, supporting the professional development and skill growth of the enrollment team. Maintain comprehensive, current Slate documentation and establish new documentation for all evolving business processes. Participate in professional development opportunities, including virtual and in-person Slate community events and conferences. Develop, facilitate, and expand comprehensive training opportunities for the enrollment team regarding Slate features, ensuring staff across the division are proficient, empowered, and utilizing the CRM to its highest capacity. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Data Science, Information Technology, Analytics, Business Intelligence, Higher Education, or a related field. Minimum of 5–7 years of professional experience in higher education enrollment management, admissions operations, or enrollment analytics. 3–5 years of demonstrated experience as a key member/administrator of a Technolutions Slate team, with deep competency in configuration, workflows, and queries. Demonstrated experience supervising, mentoring, or leading professional staff and managing complex projects. Experience utilizing computer databases for admissions and a strong understanding of data exchange protocols. Competency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Access) and Google Suite. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to present complex technical and analytical information clearly to diverse audiences. Demonstrates good judgment, discretion, and a commitment to building an inclusive environment and effective partnerships across the university. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in a related field. Advanced experience writing and optimizing queries, building predictive models, and managing complex integrations. Strong familiarity with Banner SIS and/or experience executing a data transition to Workday is highly preferred. Experience with specialized enrollment technologies, document imaging, and external application platforms (e.g., Common Application). Advanced analytical and critical thinking skills with a proven track record of converting complex datasets into actionable institutional strategies. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."
    },
    "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Director-of-Residence-Life_JR100170": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Residence Life",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Assistant Director provides on-campus support to a 2200 bed community. The Assistant Director serves as the primary coordinator of residential programming, departmental assessment, training initiatives and electronic/web communication. This position is live-on. A fully furnished university apartment that includes utilities is provided. Residence Life experience required. Job Description : - Serve as an ambassador/liaison for the Office of Residence Life and Division of Student Affairs. - Assist Director with development/implementation of annual goals, training initiatives, calendar development, assessment strategies and fulfilling department/division objectives. - Oversee the recruitment, selection, training and supervision of all para-professional staff (Resident Directors, Senior Resident Assistants, & Resident Assistants) & summer staff (ex. Clery Act compliance, systems operation, check-in & check-outs, etc.). - Implement campus wide programming initiatives for traditional and non-traditional populations. - Develop marketing initiatives for the office via social media and advertisements. - Assist with Homecoming planning. -Assist in the development and administration of assessment initiatives for the Office of Residence Life in connection with department/division/campus wide Student Learning Outcomes. - Coordinate and implement paraprofessional staff training initiatives for Division of Student Affairs. - Serve on designated committees and initiatives for the division of Student Affairs. - Work directly with web-based housing software (e.g. room selection, reports, etc.). - Manage and update the Office of Residence Life webpage and other social media outlets. - Attend weekly residence life staff meeting with 12 paraprofessional Resident Directors. - Co-facilitate opening and closing of residential areas and other administrative functions. - Fulfill responsibilities of the Director and Housing Coordinator in his/her absence. - Develop and coordinate desk operations where applicable. - Provide on-call coverage as the Professional Staff On-Call on a rotating basis with Director. - Serve as a core member of the Care Team, reaching out to students and completing wellness checks, and attending weekly Care Team meetings - Availability to work evenings and weekends as needed. -Interpersonal Communication & Public Speaking ability. - Other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."
    },
    "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assistant-Director-of-Academic-Success--Rank-of-Instructor_JR100141": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Academic Success; Rank of Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Assistant Director of Academic Success. Non-tenure Track Faculty. 12-month appointment with eligibility for continuing appointment. Instructor Status. The Ohio Northern University Pettit College of Law is seeking to appoint an Assistant Director of Academic Success. Job Description : The Assistant Director will lead the academic support program at ONU and coordinate with and report to the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs to provide an integrated program of academic support and bar support services. The Assistant Director will be an integral part of the Academic Success Program (ASP) at Ohio Northern University College of Law, working with the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and the Assistant Director for Bar Passage by: Designing and implementing strategies to successfully assist all students' learning, particularly in areas of essay writing, reading comprehension, issue spotting, and legal analysis; Designing and implementing strategies to successfully assist at-risk and high-risk students through individual instruction and by teaching academic support-related courses, including hosting weekly ASP sessions in the Summer Starter Program; Assisting in designing and implementing the academic support component of orientation programs and coordinating and teaching in the January term to first-year students; Hiring, training, and supervising the teaching assistants in the ASP; Evaluating and creating, along with other members of the administration, reports on statistical data regarding students' academic performance and providing input regarding the effectiveness of ASP programs and initiatives. Required Skills: Strong writing, analytical, and organizational skills Strong interpersonal skills including the ability to communicate with groups of students Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must hold at least a J.D. from an ABA accredited law school with a minimum of more than one year’s prior experience in academic support. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."
    },
    "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Assessment-Coordinator_JR100120": {
      "title": "Assessment Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Academic Assessment Coordinator collects, catalogs, and analyzes assessment data for the college of pharmacy. Job Description : Maintain the Curricular map Prepare, maintain, and assist with analysis assessment data and reports for College of Pharmacy curricula, including but not limited to: didactic coursework, IPPE, APPE, IPE, Co-Curricular, Assessment days Collaborate with faculty and staff on curricular and assessment items for the college Prepare verbal and written reports on assessment information for faculty and staff Assist in preparation for and execution of ACPE accreditation Assist in preparation of reports for University Assessment/HLC accreditation Support professional development and co-curriculum courses Complete special projects as they relate to assessment in the College of Pharmacy Other duties as assigned   Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."
