    "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Advanced-Administrative-Assistant_JR100123": {
      "title": "Advanced Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: The Advanced Administrative Assistant provides comprehensive administrative support to the Office of Law Career Services & Student Services and the College of Law faculty. This position coordinates career services initiatives while serving as a primary resource for faculty, students, alumni, employers, and other external constituents. This position requires exceptional organizational skills, attention to detail, discretion, and the ability to manage multiple priorities while providing outstanding customer service to faculty, staff, and students. Job Description : Career & Professional Development Support Research and identify employment opportunities, internships, clerkships, and networking opportunities for law students and alumni. Review and approve employer job postings to ensure compliance with college recruiting policies and maintain the integrity of the online career management system. Provide training and assistance to students, alumni, employers, and faculty in the use of the 12twenty career management platform. Coordinate and provide training for the OSCAR (Online System for Clerkship Application and Review) federal judicial clerkship application system. Process reciprocity requests with other law schools' career services offices. Assist in planning, promoting, and executing fundraising initiatives and scholarship programs that support public interest employment. Maintain accurate employment, employer, and recruiting records for reporting and accreditation purposes. Event & Program Coordination Coordinate logistics for employer recruitment programs, networking events, student workshops, alumni programs, faculty meetings, and other special events. Prepare meeting materials, agendas, correspondence, and follow-up communications for departmental initiatives. Assist with promotion and marketing of Career & Professional Development programs through email, website updates, and printed materials. Administrative Support Prepare, proofread, copy, and distribute documents as requested by faculty. Order and maintain office and classroom supplies, including monitoring inventory of printer paper and other essential materials. Manage departmental purchasing records, payment requests, travel reimbursements, and purchasing card reconciliation. Maintain welcoming, organized, and professional office, reception, interview, conference, and hospitality spaces. Serve as the first point of contact for students, faculty, alumni, employers, and visitors by answering inquiries and directing requests appropriately. Office & Facilities Coordination Assist with setting up offices for new faculty members. Reserve classrooms and meeting spaces for faculty, staff, and students. Submit work orders to Physical Plant for maintenance and facility needs. Coordinate printer service requests and other equipment maintenance. Distribute incoming mail and departmental correspondence. Records Management Maintain organized electronic and physical records related to academic courses and faculty activities. Ensure accurate filing and retention of academic documents in shared departmental drives. Maintain confidentiality of student and faculty records in accordance with university policies and applicable regulations. Faculty & Academic Support Create and maintain faculty course folders each academic term, including class rosters, attendance sheets, exam numbers, syllabi, and examination documents. Upload and post first-week assignments to the College of Law website. Order required course textbooks and coordinate with the university bookstore to ensure timely availability. Prepare and maintain faculty advising schedules and appointment sign-up sheets. Save and archive final examinations and course materials according to established departmental procedures. Assist faculty with entering final grades into the university's student information system. Submit semester book award information for top-performing students. Examination Administration Coordinate the administration of Exam4 and Scantron examinations for midterms and final exams. Prepare examination files and answer keys. Operate scanning equipment and examination software to process Scantron exams. Export examination data and maintain accurate testing records. Ensure examination materials are organized, secure, and properly archived. Qualifications High School Diploma or GED Three to five years of administrative support experience, preferably in higher education or a professional office. Strong proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, including Word, Excel, and Outlook. Ability to learn and effectively use university software systems and databases. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Exceptional organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines. Strong attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to work independently while maintaining effective working relationships with faculty, staff, and students. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment in handling sensitive information. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong customer service orientation. Excellent time management and prioritization skills. Ability to troubleshoot administrative and technology-related issues. Demonstrated initiative and flexibility in a fast-paced academic environment. Ability to adapt to changing priorities throughout the academic year. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."
    },
    "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Tilton-Hall-Of-Law/Assistant-Professor-of-Law_JR100080": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Law",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Ohio Northern University's Pettit College of Law seeks candidates for three full-time, entry-level faculty positions on the tenure track. The College of Law has interest in a variety of teaching areas, including but not limited to Contracts, Sales, Secured Transactions, Property, Criminal Law, Criminal Procedure, and Evidence, and qualified lateral candidates will also be considered. ONU Law is a closely knit community focused on preparing practice-ready lawyers, with an Advocacy program ranked among the best in the nation by U.S. News & World Report. Job Description : Ohio Northern University's Pettit College of Law seeks candidates for three full-time, entry-level faculty positions on the tenure track. The College of Law has interest in a variety of teaching areas, including but not limited to Contracts, Sales, Secured Transactions, Property, Criminal Law, Criminal Procedure, and Evidence. Qualified lateral candidates will also be considered. Ohio Northern is a private university affiliated with the United Methodist Church, and its Pettit College of Law is a closely knit community built around small classes and individualized faculty mentoring. For more than 140 years, ONU Law has focused its educational mission on preparing practice-ready lawyers, an emphasis reflected in our clinical and externship placements and an Advocacy program ranked among the best in the nation by U.S. News & World Report. ONU Law is also home to one of the nation's first fully online part-time JD program accredited by the ABA. Candidates with experience as a practicing lawyer, judicial clerk, or law teacher are preferred, and we welcome candidates who bring a range of teaching interests and approaches, including experience with varied instructional formats and delivery methods. Expectations include a normal teaching load of four courses per year, scholarly research and publication, and service obligations for the 2027-2028 academic year. Candidates must have a J.D. from a law school accredited by the A.B.A. or an equivalent degree from a foreign institution, a distinguished academic record, and a commitment to excellence in teaching and scholarship. Ohio Northern University was founded in 1871, and ONU Law has been educating lawyers since 1885. Ohio Northern is located in Ada, Ohio, a quiet college community known for its small-town charm, about an hour from the growing Columbus metro area, and is home to five colleges and about 3,140 students representing 50 states and 15 countries. Ohio Northern University offers a competitive salary package commensurate with the candidate's experience and skills. Fringe benefits include the TIAA-CREF retirement program, medical insurance, disability benefits, life insurance, tuition remission for dependents attending Ohio Northern University for an initial baccalaureate degree, and eligibility for participation in The Tuition Exchange, a program involving over 640 member colleges and universities. Interested candidates are strongly encouraged to apply quickly to ensure immediate review. Interested applicants should send a curriculum vitae, official transcripts from all colleges and educational institutions attended, and the names and contact information of three professional references who have recent knowledge of the applicant's background and potential to Professor Melissa Kidder, Chair, Personnel Committee, at  m-kidder@onu.edu , College of Law, Ohio Northern University, 525 S. Main Street, Ada, OH 45810. Equal Opportunity Employer. Interested applicants are encouraged to review the ONU Law website at law.onu.edu. Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."
    },
    "https://onu.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ohio-Northern-University/Advancement-Services-Coordinator_JR100116": {
      "title": "Advancement Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCareer Opportunities at Ohio Northern University Job Summary: Supports Department of Advancement Services in Gift Processing, Biographic Data maintenance and entry, Data Integration with third-party systems, special projects, and fulfills cross-department needs as necessary. Functioning as part of the Advancement Services team, the Advancement Services Coordinator is responsible for maintaining the accuracy and integrity of the Ohio Northern University donor database to support the reporting and technical functions of the Office of Advancement. Several of the main tasks include posting incoming gifts, producing gift acknowledgments, recording gift pledges, updating and creating a variety of records regularly, maintaining campaign attainments, and preparing comparative, analytical and statistical reports. The individual will perform primary-level functions of the above activities, particularly in the electronic deposit and reconciliation of gifts, referencing existing, updating, and creating constituent records. The Advancement Services Coordinator will also assist the overall Advancement division with special projects and cross-department needs as required. Job Description : Post incoming gifts to the University in the integrated administrative database (e.g. Raiser's Edge, GiveCampus, etc.) Perform daily electronic deposits of checks through the institution’s banking portal Reconcile deposits with actual totals Produce gift acknowledgments and relevant reporting for fundraising and administrative staff, daily. Record gift pledges in Raiser's Edge and generate pledge reminders. Build a daily gift transaction log Accurately input appeals related to gifts received via specific efforts Record notes donors may have communicated Create new constituent records New alumni management Prepare annual gift statements Payroll deduction pledge and gift management Process matching gifts forms and act as liaison with matching gift corporations and related foundations Organize accompanying hardcopy materials that enable seamless logging of gifts in Raiser's Edge Collaborate in the continuous effort to improve the quality and accuracy of data (including the development and modification of department data standards, implementing more automated processes for consistency, etc.). Perform a variety of updates on including records: Contact information Marital information Occupational/Business ownership history Additional Familial information; children and relatives Collect and organize self-submitted profile updates from ONU’s alumni system in preparation for mass updates Special projects to enhance data health Research “lost” and deceased alumni to maintain current contact profiles that enable appropriate communication Utilize Internet search, electronic and hardcopy data to confirm, update or resolve inconsistencies in constituent profile data Create and Maintain Reports/Information Provide tools and documentation for annual audits, in conjunction with the University Controller Produce and monitor the integrity of monthly comparative gift reports and ensure all are maintained according to business rules and practices Maintain numerous campaign attainments as necessary Create and maintain endowed and non-endowed funds Communication and Supervision Gather factual information from within the department and from other departments. Occasionally correspond with internal and external contacts to respond to inquiries or convey the enforcement of regulations, policies, and procedures Assist in the supervision of student workers Participate in the support of division-wide or cross-departmental initiatives Act as point of contact with internal and external audiences for the department’s phone and email Other duties as assigned. Required Skills: Excellent organization and written/oral communication skills Proficiency in Microsoft Office products Ability to identify and resolve issues, analyze data, and make recommendations Forward-thinking with the ability to analyze, prioritize and improve department workflows related to data and reporting Strong attention to detail Ability to work with accuracy in a fast paced environment Above-average typing skills and excellent proof-reading skills Must be comfortable and accurate in working with numbers Highest standards of integrity and confidentiality Minimum Qualifications: Associate's degree or equivalent experience Ability to work during the end of organization's fiscal year (late May through early June), as well as, the end of the calendar year one to three years of similar office experience Preferred Qualifications  Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience Experience working in Raiser's Edge Two to Five years of similar office experience Your next professional chapter begins here! ONU is an equal employment opportunity employer. Accordingly, no person shall be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, transgender status, religion, national origin, age, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. This policy applies to all areas of employment including recruitment, hiring, training and development, promotion, transfer, compensation, benefits, discipline, separation and other terms, condition and privileges of employment."
    },
